Implemented the fix and verified `cargo test` passes.

## Root cause

Bare frontmatter is handled by `wrap_bare_frontmatter()` in `crates/liwe/src/markdown.rs`, which wraps a leading bare metadata block in synthetic `---` fences so `pulldown-cmark` parses it as YAML metadata.

That function was filtering out every line starting with a space:

```rust
.lines()
.filter(|l| !l.starts_with(' '))
```

So this bare frontmatter:

```yaml
title: Task A
depends:
  - foo
  - bar
```

was transformed into effectively:

```yaml
title: Task A
depends:
```

The `depends` sequence items were silently dropped before YAML parsing. As a result, `DocumentFinder::metadata_matches()` had no sequence values to match, so `iwe find --meta depends=foo` returned no results.

Fenced YAML worked because it bypassed `wrap_bare_frontmatter()`.

## Fix

Changed `wrap_bare_frontmatter()` to preserve indented YAML lines and only trim trailing whitespace from the whole header before inserting synthetic fences:

```rust
let header = header.trim_end();
if rest.is_empty() {
    Cow::Owned(format!("---\n{}\n---\n", header))
} else {
    Cow::Owned(format!("---\n{}\n---\n\n{}", header, rest))
}
```

## Regression test

Added a regression test in `crates/liwe/tests/find_metadata_test.rs` for bare frontmatter sequence matching:

```rust
#[test]
fn bare_frontmatter_value_in_yaml_sequence_matches() {
    let graph = setup_bare_graph(indoc! {"
        title: Task A
        depends:
          - foo
          - bar

        # Task A
    "});

    let finder = DocumentFinder::new(&graph);
    let options = FindOptions {
        metadata_filters: vec![("depends".to_string(), "foo".to_string())],
        ..Default::default()
    };
    let output = finder.find(&options);
    assert_eq!(output.results.len(), 1);
    assert_eq!(output.results[0].title, "Task A");
}
```

